do CelyneLoop.play_bgm()
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/PART OF YOUR WORLD.png" fade="0.0"]
join Seyche left
join Celyna center
As days blurred into hours for the goddesses, an unexpected warmth enveloped them. Unforced and achingly familiar. It was as if it had always lingered there, waiting. Waiting patiently for a thousand years.
The sea lit up with a brilliant blue glow, like stars dancing along with the waves like reflections of the night sky. They sat by the shore, side by side, admiring the view above and before them.
Seyche’s eyes never left Celyna, marveling at details of the moon goddess’s features. The twinkle in her hair, the way her graceful form complimented the night. How the light of her presence balanced the shadows, as if the galaxies itself leaned in to admire her.
Celyna: Is there something you wish to ask, dear?
update Seyche (Surprised) [fade="Fade Cross" fade_length="0.0"]
Seyche: !!
Seyche: Wha- no! I mean... no, sorry. I was...
Celyna: No need to apologize.
Celyna: Though it seems like you have something in your mind.
Seyche (Uncomfortable): Oh… I was just… thinking.
Celyna: Of what, dear?
The sea goddess took a pause, the question seemed so simple yet she couldn’t really say what she had in mind. Because really, even though they had just first met, everything seemed so familiar. But she had no recollection of anything.
The days spent together felt effortless, as though it had always been that way. Seyche didn’t answer right away, she only shook her head, brushing away her thoughts while shifting her gaze towards the view before her.
Seyche (Happy): I forgot about it already.
An occasional chuckle came from Celyna after Seyche’s reply before returning to their comfortable silence. Some things don't always change from the past.
At least...
That’s what Celyna hoped.